=== PARITY (web source reproduced end-to-end) ===
  Web body (the entire component):
      const TAB_TO_ROUTE = {
        alerts:      '/notifications/alerts',
        history:     '/notifications/inbox',
        preferences: '/notifications/quiet-hours',
      };
      const params = new URLSearchParams(location.search);
      const tab    = params.get('tab') ?? 'alerts';
      params.delete('tab');
      const target = TAB_TO_ROUTE[tab] ?? '/notifications/alerts';
      const to     = qs ? `${target}?${qs}` : target;
      return <Navigate to={to} replace />;
  Native mapping (one-for-one):
    - useLocation()               -> LegacyAlertsRedirectSource (P1/S8 seam; no HTTP in view)
    - URLSearchParams(search)     -> Resolver.parseQuery (ordered URLQueryItem, leading '?' tolerated)
    - params.get('tab') ?? alerts -> AlertsRedirectTab(tabParameter:) — first `tab`, missing→alerts
    - params.delete('tab')        -> forwardedItems = items.filter { name != "tab" } (drops EVERY entry)
    - TAB_TO_ROUTE[tab] ?? alerts -> AlertsRedirectTab per-tab paths + unknown-string→alerts (usedFallback)
    - qs ? target?qs : target     -> ResolvedAlertsRedirect.target (bare path when nothing forwarded)
    - <Navigate to replace/>      -> LegacyAlertsRedirectRouter.replace(with:) dispatched ONCE on mount
  TAB_TO_ROUTE parity asserted (note the RENAMES — the key differentiator from sibling 0187):
    alerts→/notifications/alerts, history→/notifications/INBOX, preferences→/notifications/QUIET-HOURS;
    fallback /notifications/alerts. Verified by a real Swift run of all 9 routes (GATE RESULTS).

=== STATES (every state renders — never a blank box) ===
  The web spec's generic state list maps onto a SYNCHRONOUS redirect (useLocation
  is router state, not a network resource — there is no loading/error/stale/offline
  data envelope). Reproduced honestly:
    - resolving  : transient redirect affordance (ProgressView + label) — the native
                   stand-in for the web's invisible/instant <Navigate>. (= "loading")
    - redirecting: resolved destination + chip + manual "Continue" fallback so the
                   redirect is actionable even if auto-nav was not honored. (= "loaded")
    - alerts default/fallback (web `?? alerts`): friendly "Showing your alerts" note —
                   the "empty/default" branch, rendered, never blank.
  There is deliberately NO fabricated error/stale/offline surface: the web source
  has no async data source to fail, go stale, or go offline. (Documented in the
  Phase enum.) Every branch is exercised by the #if DEBUG previews + the tests.

